Subject: Align Knative 1.23 resource schema with the bumped OpenTelemetry SDK
Origin: DHI-internal (OpenTelemetry resource initialization compatibility)
Base-Tree: git https://github.com/knative/serving 7ed4aa2ab601e3a33c6552285f6e0d910747351d
Verify: test tests/testdata/observability_startup_test.go::TestDHIObservabilityStartup
Forwarded: not-needed (compatibility with DHI dependency bumps)
Drop-When: never: required while this release's Knative resource schema differs from the bumped SDK default

Knative 1.23 creates resources with semconv v1.41.0, while SDK v1.45.0 creates its default resource with v1.43.0. Merging them panics in resource.Default during component startup. Retarget the Knative wrapper to the SDK's schema so resource attributes can merge without a conflicting schema URL.

diff --git a/vendor/knative.dev/pkg/observability/semconv/semconv.go b/vendor/knative.dev/pkg/observability/semconv/semconv.go
--- a/vendor/knative.dev/pkg/observability/semconv/semconv.go
+++ b/vendor/knative.dev/pkg/observability/semconv/semconv.go
@@ -18,7 +18,7 @@
 
 import (
 	"go.opentelemetry.io/otel/attribute"
-	semconv "go.opentelemetry.io/otel/semconv/v1.41.0"
+	semconv "go.opentelemetry.io/otel/semconv/v1.43.0"
 )
 
 const (
